    <description>Quick Action screen flow on Opportunity (LFRDN-343 / ALF-RS-13). Captures cancellation reason, evidence, and notes, blocks re-submission when already Cancelled or already Pending approval, sets AF_CancellationApprovalStatus__c = Pending, creates the linked AF_CreditNote__c (Pending, Reason=Cancellation) which auto-submits into AF_AP_CreditNote_Cancellation via the existing AF_FL_CreditNote_SubmitApproval, then submits the Opportunity itself for approval via AF_AP_Opp_Cancellation (Owner&apos;s Manager). Same manager-hierarchy submission pattern as AF_FL_Opp_RequestClosure / AF_FL_Opp_RequestInternalRequisition.

LFRDN-728 fix: the Manager_Can_See_Deal block screen already existed (a real, correct fail-safe for the LFRDN-707-style cross-BU access gap), but it only ever blocked - it never actually got the manager access to approve. Added Share_Opportunity_With_Manager (same OpportunityShare/Edit/Manual pattern as LFRDN-707) right after the manager is resolved, before the UserRecordAccess check - so the manager now has access before that check even runs, and Screen_ManagerCannotApprove becomes a pure safety net rather than the default outcome for any cross-BU manager.

LFRDN-728 QA-rejected re-fix (2026-09-28, per Marwan): Get_Manager_Record_Access used storeOutputAutomatically with no queriedFields - UserRecordAccess requires RecordId to be explicitly selected, which automatic output storage silently omitted, so the lookup faulted with &quot;RecordId field must be selected&quot; on every single submission (breaking Cancel Sales Order entirely) and had no faultConnector to catch it. Switched to explicit queriedFields (RecordId, HasReadAccess) + storeOutputAutomatically=false + an explicit outputAssignments into Var_ManagerHasReadAccess (Salesforce requires a manual output variable once storeOutputAutomatically is false, confirmed via a real failed deploy trying to keep the old Get_Manager_Record_Access.HasReadAccess reference), and added a faultConnector to Screen_Error so any future lookup failure surfaces a real message instead of an unhandled fault.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>AF_Formula_CreditNoteAmount</name>
        <dataType>Currency</dataType>
        <expression>IF(ISBLANK({!Get_Opportunity.AF_InvoiceSummary__r.AF_PaidAmount__c}), 0, {!Get_Opportunity.AF_InvoiceSummary__r.AF_PaidAmount__c})</expression>
        <scale>2</scale>
    </formulas>
